    "category": "Backtracking",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer N, construct the lexicographically largest sequence satisfying: \u2022 Number 1 appears once. \u2022 Every integer 2...N appears twice. \u2022 The two occurrences of i are separated by exactly i positions.",
